@@ -0,0 +1,39 @@
+# Track objects and palette refinement
+
+Owner request, 2026-10-12: review every track object, refine the overly simple models, and improve the menu icons, with AAA as the quality target.
+
+Requirements: TO01 — all 34 placeable families / 37 variants; TO02 — legible, coherent icons of the actual models; TO03 — unchanged canonical collision, hazards, movement, placement, undo and saves; TO04 — consistent restrained cel-shaded pigment on Compatibility and Mobile; TO05 — bounded caching and measured desktop cost; TO06 — actual captures and explicit remaining owner/device acceptance. Preserve V04-V06/G01/R01/Q01 and the existing speed-bump, continuous-barrier and winter contracts.
+
+The original shared kit now has tapered trunks and visible branching, layered leaf masses, folded grass blades, flower petals, fractured stones/outcrops, cliff scree and log bark/end grain. Track furniture uses Jersey concrete profiles, folded guardrail sections, diamond wire mesh, timber joints, framed signs, moulded cones, shaped lamp housings and a lattice start gantry. Crates have planks/braces/nails, pallets have forklift gaps, steel drums have hoops and bungs, and containers have corrugations, corner castings, hinges and locking bars. Fictional service vehicles have cut wheel arches, round tyres/rims, panel seams, separate glazing, lights and bumpers; the wreck has rust panels, exposed components and a missing wheel. Garage/marshal buildings have framed openings, roof edges, gutters and roller-door detail; the grandstand has individual seats, an aisle, stairs and support/rail construction. Tyre stacks have rounded carcasses, open beads, shoulder ribs and tread cuts. Jumps and speed bumps retain their existing profiles with cosmetic seams, reinforcement and fixings. Oil and the legacy puddle have restrained broken liquid sheen.
+
+All 37 menu variants use these same shipping model builders. The icons now have 384x232 one-shot studio renders, tuned framing for tall and flat objects, warm key/cool fill lighting, soft contact shading and mipmapped baked textures. The existing 104x82 controls, actions and captions remain. The legacy dirt and pond stamps were also audited: they are canonical terrain/surface stamps, not independent models, and retain the established biome surface presentation. No new placeable kind, dependency, external art, brand, runtime API or player-facing explanation was added. All geometry and the preview shader are original project-authored assets.
+
+Authored vertex colours are treated as sRGB in the prop materials, including snow-covered props. The hazard shader converts those pigments for Mobile's linear lighting while keeping Compatibility's sRGB output. This fixes the washed-out Mobile rubber/foliage/oil revealed by the first comparison. Road/terrain material colour handling is outside this change. Local unindexed model sources are cached (96 entries; pine colour variants 32) and indexed after assembly; thumbnails keep their existing 48-image limit and release the 3D viewport after baking. The track presentation revision was advanced for cache invalidation; concurrent road presentation revisions are preserved separately in the scoped checkpoint.
+
+Runtime files: `game/track/creator_prop_visual.gd`, new `prop_geometry.gd`, `prop_nature.gd`, `prop_equipment.gd`, `prop_structures.gd` (+UIDs), the object/tyre/material sections of `native_track_visual.gd`, `hazard_visual.gd`, `hazard.gdshader`, the pigment setting in `winter_scenery.gd`, `game/editor/object_thumbnail.gd`, and new `prop_preview_shadow.gdshader` (+UID). Tests: new `test_prop_refinement.gd`, `capture_prop_refinement.gd`, `profile_prop_refinement.gd` (+UIDs), plus graphical frame-lifetime waits in `test_moving_prop_presentation.gd`, with every previous assertion retained. Documentation: this file, `AGENTS.md`, `DEVELOPMENT_STATUS.md`, `docs/PHASE_0_PLAN.md`.
+
+Actual commands use the pinned `4.7.2.stable.official.ed1daf0bf` through `powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/dev.ps1`:
+
+| Arguments | Actual result |
+| --- | --- |
+| `-Action CaptureObjectModels` | Before and iterative after captures, 37 variants; gameplay collision cells unchanged. |
+| `-Action TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_prop_refinement.gd` | 579 checks, zero failures: 38 rendered kinds (including legacy puddle) across all five biomes, finite meshes/normals, outward primitive normals, bounded geometry/cache, cached transforms/run lengths, and exact unchanged document/collision data. |
+| Same prop test with `-Graphical -RenderingMethod mobile -RenderingDriver vulkan` | 579 checks, zero failures on actual desktop Mobile mesh buffers. |
+| `-Action TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/capture_prop_refinement.gd -Graphical` and the same with `-RenderingMethod mobile -RenderingDriver vulkan` | 144 checks per renderer, zero failures. Pigment measurements are retained in the evidence logs; they include all 37 unclipped nonblank icons, mipmaps, viewport disposal, cache reuse and actual editor controls at 1280x720 / 960x540. |
+| `-Action TestObjects`, `-Action TestHazards`, `-Action TestCompilerRaster` | 67, 157 and 8 checks respectively; zero failures. Raster goldens were not rewritten. |
+| `-Action TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_speed_bump_width.gd` | 362 checks, zero failures; independent span and crown/visual bounds retained. |
+| `-Action TestCreator`, `-Action TestApp` | 113 and 99 checks respectively; zero failures. The creator's explicit historical three-lap diagnostic fixture is unchanged; ordinary races remain five laps. |
+| `-Action TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_moving_prop_presentation.gd -Graphical -TestArgument '--capture-moving-props=res://../docs/evidence/track-object-refinement-2026-10-12/moving'` and Mobile with `moving-mobile` | 37 checks per renderer, zero failures: actual car collisions, fresh/cached scenery, exact snapshot preservation, restored earlier states, finish coasting, restart and playground safety. |
+| `-Action TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/profile_prop_refinement.gd -Graphical` and Mobile equivalent | Actual isolated 120-prop desktop stress measurements and scene PNGs saved per renderer. |
+| `-Action TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_script_parse.gd` | Final complete parse: 574 scripts, zero failures. |
+| `-Action Doctor` | Pinned engine/templates found; attached-device list empty. |
+
+Evidence: [all 37 icons](evidence/track-object-refinement-2026-10-12/gl_compatibility/all-37-icons.png), [Mobile icons](evidence/track-object-refinement-2026-10-12/mobile/all-37-icons.png), [compact building menu](evidence/track-object-refinement-2026-10-12/gl_compatibility/editor-buildings-960.png), [compact prop menu](evidence/track-object-refinement-2026-10-12/mobile/editor-props-960.png), [track furniture](evidence/track-object-refinement-2026-10-12/gl_compatibility/models-trackside.png). Each renderer folder includes five model stages, ten actual editor screens, `icon-pigments.json`, `profile.json` and the stress capture; the moving folders contain actual before/after impact screenshots. Initial before sources/images, actual success/failure logs, scoped patch and hash ledger are preserved under the same evidence root. The isolated two-commit Git review checkpoint is `build/track_object_refinement/checkpoint-repo`; it preserves the main repository branch/index and unrelated concurrent work.
+
+The measured stage contains 142,990 triangles and 31 geometry nodes for 120 props plus a neutral floor. It excludes roads, HUD, particles and driving; desktop RTX 3090 render costs and cold/warm construction times are in each `profile.json`. Final Compatibility CPU median/p95: 0.322/0.479 ms, GPU: 0.760/1.795 ms, cold/warm construction: 330.554 / 207.207 / 192.700 ms. Mobile CPU: 0.129/0.193 ms, GPU: 0.771/0.869 ms, construction: 405.780 / 250.267 / 270.030 ms. These are not whole-game frame times, phone results, a demonstrated improvement over the previous kit, or a thermal test. Individual default models have 60–4,920 triangles; the six-stack tyre-wall variant has 7,200. Mobile budgets and larger authored populations still need physical-device measurement.
+
+Initial corrections are recorded rather than counted as passes: normal/cap winding, mixed indexed/unindexed append omission, and diagnostic stage clipping were fixed. The moving-prop fixture initially freed scenes before their queued callbacks ran; actual graphical frame waits fix its lifetime without removing or weakening any assertions. Initial direct-script execution was blocked by Windows execution policy, and sandboxed Godot/ADB could not write their normal local logs; the project entry point was rerun with authorized normal local execution. A later import encountered a locked Windows audio extension during concurrent project work; the subsequent app smoke check passed after the new Garage class registered. The first broader all-script parse encountered an audio capture superclass error during concurrent work; its final retry passed all 574 scripts.
+
+The existing `test_biomes.gd` has five failing “New repeats required selection with fresh identity” assertions: the editor now opens its unsaved-change confirmation before replacing a document, while that fixture expects immediate navigation. The other 102 checks passed. This pass does not change that workflow or weaken those assertions; its separate all-biome prop checks pass. This is not a clean full-project Validate result.
+
+No Android export/install, physics change/merge, full replay suite, backend operation, deployment or live account write was performed for this task. No phone is attached and no physical-device test was performed. Owner review remains for silhouettes, palette/icon recognition and the overall quality target; physical acceptance remains for touch readability, camera occlusion, dense-object motion, sustained memory/frame pacing and thermals. Restart the client to load the refined kit. This is a completed local object-presentation pass, not a claim that the entire game has achieved AAA quality.
